From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mio <mio@mio19.uk>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:53:34 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] android-init-boot-timeout: bound android-init shutdown

Android init's stop waits for the vendor modem to acknowledge power-down,
which never happens on this device (bgcom_dev "Time out on modem down
event", then pil-q6v5-mss halt timeouts), so with the Bluetooth HAL running
every reboot sat on a blank screen for the default 90s TimeoutStopSec
before systemd SIGKILLed the Android cgroup. Bound the stop job to 15s;
the same SIGKILL now arrives 75s sooner and the reboot still completes
cleanly.
---
 devices/fossil-hoki/android-init.nix | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/devices/fossil-hoki/android-init.nix b/devices/fossil-hoki/android-init.nix
index 43d21df0..14061645 100644
--- a/devices/fossil-hoki/android-init.nix
+++ b/devices/fossil-hoki/android-init.nix
@@ -103,6 +103,14 @@ in
     unitConfig.Conflicts = [ "shutdown.target" ];
     serviceConfig = {
       Type = "simple";
+      # Android init's shutdown waits for the vendor modem to acknowledge
+      # power-down, which never happens on this device (bgcom_dev
+      # "Time out on modem down event", then pil-q6v5-mss "halt timeout").
+      # Without a bound the stop job sits for the default 90 s, so a reboot
+      # looks hung on a blank screen until systemd finally SIGKILLs the
+      # whole Android cgroup. Bound it instead; the kernel gets the same
+      # SIGKILLed init either way, just 75 s sooner.
+      TimeoutStopSec = "15s";
       ExecStartPre = pkgs.writeShellScript "android-init-pre" ''
         ln_force() {
           local target="$1"
